1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Sunday noon, the Mo family living room. Three hours before Uncle's blind date.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:10,800
My type is simple. 175 cm or taller, baby-faced, great conversation, big salary, nice personality.

3
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,033
Simple? Aren't your standards too high?

4
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:17,200
Too high? That's baseline! So what!

5
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,467
Sir. Before the date, I'll check just one thing.

6
00:00:20,467 --> 00:00:21,833
Huh? When did you get here?!

7
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:25,467
It's our appointment time. Sir, where is YOUR checklist?

8
00:00:25,467 --> 00:00:27,300
Mine… I never wrote one.

9
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:32,600
Others' standards: too high. Mine: baseline. Double standard, number one.

10
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:35,467
I'm… Modapman.

11
00:00:35,467 --> 00:00:40,300
If I do it, so what. If you do it: awkward! The dating-hunt edition.

12
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:41,833
Round one: looks.

13
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:44,000
I don't care about looks. The heart is what matters.

14
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,300
Then why are you zooming in on her photo like that?

15
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:49,567
That's not looking at looks. That's collecting first-impression data.

16
00:00:49,567 --> 00:00:52,533
Uncle, you're looking at the eyes in the photo.

17
00:00:52,533 --> 00:00:59,633
Others look at looks: shallow. I look: data collection. Double standard, number two.

18
00:00:59,633 --> 00:01:02,533
When was your own profile photo taken?

19
00:01:02,533 --> 00:01:05,267
Ten years ago, but the vibe is exactly the same now.

20
00:01:05,267 --> 00:01:06,033
Here. A mirror.

21
00:01:06,033 --> 00:01:08,167
I… have a certain vibe.

22
00:01:08,167 --> 00:01:12,833
Zoom in on her face, never look at my mirror. Double standard, number three.

23
00:01:12,833 --> 00:01:20,367
Sir, people tend to rate themselves above average. Your date will look at you with the same eyes.

24
00:01:20,367 --> 00:01:22,633
Uncle's mirror is generous!

25
00:01:22,633 --> 00:01:25,067
Round two: age.

26
00:01:25,067 --> 00:01:30,000
Her age: 25 to 33. I'm 39, but age is just a number!

27
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,067
This one is 37. That's close to you.

28
00:01:33,067 --> 00:01:35,667
Thirty-seven? That's a bit old…

29
00:01:35,667 --> 00:01:39,833
Uncle, if thirty-seven is old, what's thirty-nine?

30
00:01:39,833 --> 00:01:41,400
…You don't need to know my age.

31
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:46,967
Peers are too old; younger people, age is just a number. Double standard, number four.

32
00:01:46,967 --> 00:01:50,200
Your standards keep climbing like a ladder.

33
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:56,133
Some research found that how much you like someone after meeting predicts more than the checklist you wrote beforehand.

34
00:01:56,133 --> 00:01:57,400
So the list is just a reference?

35
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:02,533
My age is a number; her age is a cap. Double standard, number five.

36
00:02:02,533 --> 00:02:03,967
…Does it sound like that?

37
00:02:03,967 --> 00:02:06,833
Round three: date manners, rapid fire.

38
00:02:06,833 --> 00:02:09,467
Her photo must be unedited! Mine is just lighting adjustment.

39
00:02:09,467 --> 00:02:15,267
Others edit: cheating. I edit: lighting. Double standard, number six.

40
00:02:15,267 --> 00:02:17,667
If she's fifteen minutes late, that's disrespect!

41
00:02:17,667 --> 00:02:19,300
And if you're twenty minutes late?

42
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:20,433
The road was jammed~

43
00:02:20,433 --> 00:02:26,433
Others late: rude. Me late: traffic. Double standard, number seven.

44
00:02:26,433 --> 00:02:29,633
If she replies late, she's ghosting. If I do, I'm busy.

45
00:02:29,633 --> 00:02:31,200
It's the same phone.

46
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:36,700
Others reply late: ghosting. Me: busy. Double standard, number eight.

47
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:40,233
Hey, junior! You're the guy my daughter is meeting today?!

48
00:02:40,233 --> 00:02:42,133
Senior?! A-age is just a number!

49
00:02:42,133 --> 00:02:44,967
Not my daughter. Age is NOT just a number.

50
00:02:44,967 --> 00:02:46,600
Oh my, a boomerang.

51
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:50,467
It's someone else's business… no, if it were our house…

52
00:02:50,467 --> 00:02:57,367
Someone else's daughter: age is a number. My daughter: age is NOT a number. Double standard, nine, ten.

53
00:02:57,367 --> 00:02:59,300
…Honey, it's a misunderstanding.

54
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:01,067
I haven't said anything yet.

55
00:03:01,067 --> 00:03:02,000
Just a wrong answer.

56
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,267
…Classic Modapman.
